WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.920
Robed figures with hidden faces stand over
seven young women, tied up.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.940
The robed figures chant phrases both arcane
and profane.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:14.160
The leader among these dark cultists clears
his wicked throat and says, “Be not afraid,

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:14.700
girls.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.580
You are here for something wonderful.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:22.260
To beget seven perfect children for the Scarlet
King…”

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:26.760
How did we get here, and more importantly,
what happened afterward?

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:32.040
In the near-constant darkness that follows
the grim but necessary work of the SCP Foundation,

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:37.200
there is one bright light that can always
be counted on to keep hope alive, to bring

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.960
a little sunshine into everyone's days: SCP-999,
the Tickle Monster.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:48.180
The sweet, simple creature does nothing but
provide an endless source of joy, hugging,

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.120
playing, and delighting in loving everything
around it.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:55.740
But what if I told you that this slimy little
friend has hidden depths?

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:00.780
A tragic history that seems impossible to
reconcile with the happy, playful being we

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.560
all know and love?

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:07.200
How could 999, the happiest SCP ever, have
a sad backstory?

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.200
Well, it's one of the best-kept secrets at
the Foundation.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:15.360
Before we get to that, let's talk about a
Foundation researcher and her brand new job

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:20.580
- a new job that would make her privy to some
highly classified Foundation secrets.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:25.800
Dr. Izzy Collingwood was delighted to wake
up to a call informing her that she had been

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:29.640
appointed to one of the most coveted positions
at the SCP Foundation.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:34.560
After applying, crossing her fingers, and
hoping for the best, she had been promoted

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.380
to Head Researcher for SCP-999.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:42.780
What could be better than attending to the
kindest, gentlest, cutest anomaly in Foundation

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:43.380
custody?

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:47.640
Gone were the days of coming into work and
wondering if she'd leave in one piece.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:53.160
No more cleaning up toxic spills, fighting
to contain killer creatures, or fetching cups

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:56.940
of coffee for old doctors that wouldn't give
her so much as a "thank you."

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:59.220
Years of hard work had paid off.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:03.720
Now, she could rest on her laurels and do
work that she truly enjoyed.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.300
There was just the matter&nbsp;
of some simple paperwork,&nbsp;

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.880
and she would be ready to begin this extremely

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:11.640
welcome new chapter of her professional life.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:16.380
When she walked into her office to get started
on the paperwork, something unusual caught

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:16.860
her eye.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:21.900
There was a small stack of files on her desk,
with a sticky note attached to the front.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:26.880
There were just two words written on the note,
to indicate what might await her inside the

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.320
folders: "The Truth."

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.640
She scoffed at first.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.320
"Very funny, guys!"

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.880
She called out the door.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:37.440
But no one responded, no one came forward
to take credit for the elaborate joke.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:42.060
Maybe they were playing the long game, or
maybe... she couldn't be sure.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:44.580
She sat down, flipping the first folder open.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:48.960
It was untitled, unlabeled, just plain text
on a page.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:54.300
She almost closed it after a brief scan, but
the words "The Scarlet King" jumped out at

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:54.480
her.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:59.460
She had worked at the Foundation long enough
to hear that name more than a few times, often

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:04.920
spoken in hushed tones, as if merely speaking
his name would bring about some kind of disaster.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:10.560
As she dug deeper into the file, she realized
just what she was looking at: the proposed

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.960
origins of the Scarlet King himself.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:19.620
It was a folkloric explanation, one her scientific
mind struggled to wrap around, but she had

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:24.360
seen so many strange things over the years,
things that defied all rational explanation.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:28.500
Perhaps there was some truth to be found in
the myths.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:33.660
The Scarlet King had, according to the file,
once been an elder god born from the earliest

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:37.200
days of existence, in the shadows of the Tree
of Knowledge.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:42.540
He had devoured his brothers and sisters,
growing stronger with each one he consumed.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:48.600
As his strength increased, so too did his
overwhelming pain and hate, his deep desire

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:52.020
to destroy the Tree of Knowledge and all living
creatures.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:56.940
He declared himself the king of darkness,
and, through a series of horrific events,

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:02.460
took seven unwilling brides and bound them
to him with magical seals.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:07.920
Each bride bore supernatural children, powerful,
terrible, and monstrous.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:11.460
The first bride, A'tivik, had only a few children.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:16.440
Those few were skilled strategists, exceptionally
wise in the ways of war.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:21.300
The second bride was A'ghor, overcome with
constant despair and desolation.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:27.240
Her children conquered with massive, unthinking
armies, never sated and never quelled.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:31.980
The third bride, A'distat, hated her sisters
and all she surveyed.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:35.760
The fourth bride, A'zieb, took the shape of
a great beast.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:41.640
Her children followed in her stead, and were
invulnerable, their thick hides impenetrable

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.860
by physical or magical means.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:48.780
The fifth bride was A'nuht, blessed with a
strong mind and cursed with a fragile body.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:53.040
Her children were gifted in the ways of magic,
and incredibly destructive.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:56.280
The sixth bride, A'tellif, would not speak.

00:04:56.280 --> 00:05:02.040
She kept to herself, and, like her, her children
moved in silence, disguising themselves as

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:03.000
whatever they wished.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.280
The seventh bride, however, was different.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:10.500
A'habbat was her name, the smallest of the
seven, with an unbroken spirit.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:16.200
She birthed mighty heroes that she trained
in secret, in hopes that one day they would

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:20.340
overcome her family's darkness, and topple
the King from his throne.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:25.680
All the while, the Scarlet King wages his
unholy war against all things, waiting for

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:30.000
the day he can arrive in our realm and unleash
absolute destruction.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.400
Dr. Collingwood shuddered as she finished
reading, an undeniable chill passing over

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:35.700
her.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:39.300
This definitely wasn't some kind of prank
or hazing ritual.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.220
This was something dark.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:42.360
Something real.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:46.860
She held secrets in her hands, and she couldn't
stop reading them now.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.660
She opened the next folder.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:54.000
It was a description of a cult, monitored
and raided by the SCP Foundation, called "the

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.480
Children of the Scarlet King," also known
as Group MENDES.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:02.460
During a sixteen-month investigation of the
anomalous religious group, the Foundation's

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:06.780
undercover operatives were able to ascertain
a great deal of pertinent information on the

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:06.900
group.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:10.440
What they found was troubling, and of great
concern.

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:16.560
The group had ties to several wealthy benefactors,
as well as links to extremist paranormal groups.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:22.020
Their set of beliefs was relatively simple
and disturbing: they worshipped the Scarlet

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:27.180
King, and were devoted to supporting him in
his battle to destroy the Earth and all life

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.140
as we know it.

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:33.540
The faithful who followed him in this task
would be rewarded handsomely with positions

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.520
of power in the new, hellish world.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:41.160
An initial estimate put the cult's membership
at approximately eight thousand members, a

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:44.100
quarter of whom belonged to the group's primary
branch in Alabama.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:49.440
The reporting on the cult was detailed, far
too dense, and heavily researched to be fake.

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:54.120
Again, she had the distinct feeling that someone
was trying to tip her off about something

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:57.060
the Foundation hadn't wanted to be widespread
knowledge.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:00.300
With shaky hands, she picked up the final
file.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:01.860
What awaited her inside?

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:04.440
There was only one way to find out.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:07.200
She flipped it open, and began to read.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:14.580
It was a file on an entity known as SCP-231,
specifically SCP-231-7.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:19.740
An addendum was attached to the beginning
of the file, reading: "All personnel assigned

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:26.700
to SCP-231-7 must rotate out for one month
of psychological counseling after two months

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:27.240
on-site.

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:31.500
SCP-231-7 is to be kept at an undisclosed
location.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:37.260
All personnel assigned to SCP-231 will be
transported there blindfolded from Site-19

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:42.780
by a route including no fewer than seven different
forms of transportation, including but not

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:48.420
limited to aircraft, automobile, underground
tunnel, and several we cannot discuss here.

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:53.340
Removal of the blindfold during the transport
process is grounds for immediate termination.

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:59.940
Personnel assigned to SCP-231-7 must undergo
heavy psychological testing before being cleared

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:01.080
to enter the site.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.840
Individuals must score at least 72 points&nbsp;

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:07.260
on the Milgram Obedience&nbsp;
Examination, be unmarried,

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:11.820
have no offspring, and express nothing less
than total loyalty to the Foundation.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:17.280
Normal psychological screening procedures
against Axis II disorders are waived, so long

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:22.740
as the Class-D personnel in question has the
mental capacity to carry out Procedure 110-Montauk

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:23.640
as needed.

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:30.300
Personnel who express sympathy towards SCP-231-7's
plight and/or express a desire to rescue or

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:36.000
sympathize towards SCP-231-7 will be transferred
to another project without delay.

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:39.480
Any actual rescue attempts will be met with
immediate termination.

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:45.540
Personnel who have served on the staff of
SCP-231-7's Containment Team are not required

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:47.640
to divulge that information to others.

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:54.120
No official record shall be kept of the names
of any staff assigned to SCP-231-7, nor will

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:57.240
said service appear in the personnel files
of said staff.

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:04.320
While on-site, individuals assigned to SCP-231-7
will be issued concealing helmets with integrated

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.360
voice changers to protect their identity.

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:11.280
On-site staff are not to remove said uniforms
in the presence of other staff members.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:14.880
Off-duty hours are to be spent in private
quarters alone.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:21.720
Six Class D Personnel are to be assigned to
SCP-231-7 each month for the purposes of carrying

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:23.460
out Procedure 110-Montauk.

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:28.140
Violent criminals are not to be used for this
purpose due to the possibility of accidental

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:31.260
fatality during the 110-Montauk process."

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:36.780
Dr. Collingwood swallowed the lump of dread
in her throat, her palms beginning to sweat.

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:43.440
SCP-231-7 was a young woman, retrieved during
a police raid on a warehouse owned by the

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:44.640
Children of the Scarlet King.

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:50.040
She was one of seven women found there, the
first of which went into labor 24 hours after

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:50.940
being rescued.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:53.940
She did not give birth to an ordinary child,
however.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:58.140
She gave birth to a monster that took the
lives of dozens of civilians.

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:00.300
She did not survive the birth.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:04.800
The second woman was lost shortly after, also
succumbing to the dangers of the creature

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:06.480
waiting to be born from her womb.

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:11.820
One by one, the survivors, the women chosen
by this cult to become the new brides of the

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:13.380
Scarlet King, fell.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:15.780
Soon enough, there was only one left.

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:22.680
SCP-231-7, kept contained at a Foundation
Site in a hospital bed that she could never

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:23.040
leave.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:27.240
Dr. Collingwood's stomach churned as horrible
images flooded her mind.

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:32.700
The notes from attending researchers in SCP-231's
file insisted they were doing all they could

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:37.560
to save the woman, to free her from her fate,
but that there was little they could do.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:43.500
Each birth opened a gateway from this world
to another, to a world of darkness and despair,

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:46.740
and they could not allow the final seal to
be broken.

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:51.240
Simply putting the woman out of her misery
would cause the effect to jump to a new host,

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:52.560
a new bride.

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:54.540
There was nothing to be done.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:59.280
The file fell from Dr. Collingwood's hand
as she pushed herself to her feet, running

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:00.360
out into the hallway.

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:02.040
"Who put these on my desk?"

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:05.160
She shouted, her voice echoing in the empty
hall.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:05.940
"Well?

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:06.960
What do you want from me?"

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:08.460
But no answer came.

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:13.860
Slowly, she returned to her office and sank
down into her chair, haunted by what she had

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:14.100
read.

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:18.960
She had seen horrific things in her time at
the Foundation, but nothing that had shaken

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:20.700
her to her core quite like this.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:26.160
The silence in Dr. Collingwood's office was
broken by the sound of a tinny beep, coming

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:26.940
from her computer.

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:33.180
She turned on the screen, and saw the source
of the alert: One New Message, from O5 Command.

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:35.580
What could they possibly have to say to her?

00:11:35.580 --> 00:11:38.940
Could it have something to do with the files
that had wound up on her desk?

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:44.160
She accepted the message, quickly completed
the mandatory multimodal biometric ID scan,

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:45.480
and began to read.

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:51.420
"Hello, Doctor Collingwood, and congratulations
on your new appointment as SCP-999's head

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:56.160
researcher, one of the cushiest and most enviable
assignments in the entire Foundation.

00:11:56.160 --> 00:12:02.220
SCP-999 is one of the few anomalies in our
custody who will not only never attempt to

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:06.120
harm you but will actively try to save your
life if you’re ever in any danger.

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:11.160
Though your initial reaction when receiving
this assignment was no doubt elation, you

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:15.720
may have thought it was odd that such a seemingly
low-risk position was assigned by the O5 council

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:16.200
directly.

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:20.520
If you had already heard rumors of this prior
to your assignment, you probably thought it

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:25.440
was mere nepotism; the O5s protecting their
friends and loved ones by giving them the

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:26.640
safest job possible."

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:31.380
Dr. Collingwood sat back in her chair, laughing
to herself and shaking her head.

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:36.480
She would never admit it, but she absolutely
had heard those rumors, even believed them

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:38.100
until it had happened to her.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:42.960
"Unless you are so narcissistic to think that
someone on the O5 council must be your secret

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:46.380
admirer, you’ve likely realized that this
is not the case.

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:52.920
To understand why this is our concern, you
need to know about 999’s origins.

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:57.120
You may have noticed that its file makes no
mention of where it was discovered.

00:12:57.120 --> 00:12:59.400
This is a deliberate omission.

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:04.020
If you’re not familiar with the mythology
of the Scarlet King, I suggest you read up

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:04.380
on him.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:08.520
There’s plenty of unclassified information
on him in the Foundation database.

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:13.380
All that’s relevant for now is that he is
- to the best of our knowledge - the most

00:13:13.380 --> 00:13:16.260
powerful malevolent entity in the Multiverse."

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:18.960
Her stomach dropped at the mention of The
Scarlet King.

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:22.020
She was right, this was all connected somehow.

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:26.640
She leaned forward, eyes darting across the
words with increasing intensity as she read

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:26.880
on.

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:31.080
"You've been with us since you were a research
assistant, Dr. Collingwood.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:36.180
In that time, I assume you've heard many rumors
about some of the horrific things we do here

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:39.720
at the Foundation that you've never personally
witnessed.

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:42.840
I regret to inform you that these rumors are
true.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.460
Or at least, they were.

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:50.520
A thaumaturgical cult calling itself the Children
of the Scarlet King enacted a ritual wherein

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:55.740
seven young girls became effigies for each
of the Scarlet King’s seven brides, allowing

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:57.840
them to bear his horrid offspring.

00:13:57.840 --> 00:14:03.480
How they obtained the knowledge to perform
this ritual is unclear since all we ever recovered

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:04.980
were handwritten notebooks.

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:10.800
Superficial resemblances to some Sarkic practices
has led some to speculate that the Children

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:14.700
of the Scarlet King may have some ties to
modern Sarkic cults.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:20.340
It's an interesting idea, but no concrete
evidence has ever been found to link the two.

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:23.580
Investigation into the matter is ongoing.

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:28.140
As for the ritual itself, each birth caused
more destruction than the last.

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:33.360
The writings of the cult’s priest predicted
nothing less than the Apocalypse if the Seventh

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:39.120
Bride gave birth, which could only be prevented
if Procedure 110-Montauk was performed without

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:40.980
fail each and every day.

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:47.040
To our seemingly great fortune, the notebook
contained detailed instructions on how 110-Montauk

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:48.300
was to be carried out.

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:52.620
Needless to say, we found this suspiciously
convenient.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:57.000
Why would they devise a countermeasure to
prevent the very apocalypse they were trying

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:57.660
to invoke?

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:00.720
We needed more information regarding these
entities.

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:07.020
Fortunately, our archaeologists have unearthed
numerous tablets, scrolls, and artifacts of

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:08.040
the ancient Daevas.

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:13.740
They were a sadistic and warmongering people
who were granted unholy power and knowledge

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:18.540
by the Scarlet King as a reward for the death
and suffering they caused.

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:24.060
One of the Daevite tablets in our possession,
found covered in dust and blood, was a theogony

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:26.700
for the Scarlet King and his Brides.

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:28.680
It was quite informative.

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:33.720
The information that we found most relevant
to our situation was that the Seventh Bride

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:35.460
was not like her sisters.

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:39.180
She was never completely broken by her King’s
subjugation.

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:45.060
Instead of monsters, she gave birth to great
heroes in the hopes that they would destroy

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:48.240
her sisters’ children and overthrow their
father.

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:55.020
Thus far, all have failed, but by a vote of
7 in favor, 6 against - admittedly more out

00:15:55.020 --> 00:16:00.360
of concern for Procedure 110-Montauk's lack
of viability as a long-term containment strategy

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:05.460
than out of empathy for the girl - the O5
council decided to believe that the Seventh

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:10.080
Bride still remained unbroken and that her
child would be an asset to us.

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:16.980
At the risk of causing an XK-Class End of
the World Scenario, SCP-231-7 was relieved

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:24.660
from Procedure 110-Montauk following the deaths
of SCP-231-1 through -6, and was allowed to

00:16:24.660 --> 00:16:25.260
give birth.

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:28.320
SCP-999 was the result."

00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:31.860
Dr. Collingwood gasped, her hand flying to
her mouth.

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:36.480
A Research Assistant walking by her office
paused, looking at her curiously through the

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:36.600
window.

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:40.080
She waved them off with a forced smile, and
turned back to the screen.

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:42.780
Surely she couldn't have read that correctly?

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:46.140
But, no, there it was, plain as can be:

00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:47.760
"Go ahead and read that again.

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:54.120
Be sure you understand it in all its preposterous
ridiculousness; The Tickle Monster is the

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:55.740
child of the Scarlet King.

00:16:55.740 --> 00:17:00.000
We’ve been running a counterintelligence
campaign ever since, which is why everyone

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:04.380
and their mother thinks we’ve still got
a girl strapped to a rack in a bunker somewhere.

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:05.940
Let them think that.

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:10.020
Far better for everyone that the Children
of the Scarlet King believe that they’re

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:14.400
playing us for fools than for them to know
that there is a threat to their King.

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:17.040
The girl herself is fine, by the way.

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:23.340
She was cured of the trauma from her ordeal
by SCP-999, at which point it was decided

00:17:23.340 --> 00:17:28.620
she could be returned to her family so long
as they were all given class F amnestics,

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:34.920
implanted with new identities, and relocated
to a town at least 1000 km away from the Children

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.560
of the Scarlet King's nearest known activity.

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:42.600
On the insistence of the Ethics Committee,
the family was also given a seven-figure payout

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:48.480
as compensation for our repeated…misdeeds
against their daughter, as were the families

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:50.880
of the other SCP-231s.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:54.000
I suppose it was technically malpractice on
our part.

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:58.440
In case we have any moles for the Children
of the Scarlet King in the Foundation, as

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:05.400
far as anyone else knows 231-7's family were
killed in front of her as part of 110-Montauk.

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:06.780
I’m sure you’re skeptical.

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:07.980
Are we insane?

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:12.660
How could our sweet little tickle monster
ever hope to dethrone a Lovecraftian Horror

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:13.860
of unparalleled might?

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:17.580
Well, SCP-999 is less than a decade old.

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:21.900
It’s still just a child, and nowhere near
its full strength.

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:24.300
Even so, its power is incredible.

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:28.140
Even brief interaction with&nbsp;
SCP-999 can permanently&nbsp;

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:31.200
cure severe depression and PTSD, and more

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:36.840
recent experiments have resulted in the complete
reformation of D-class personnel who were

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:39.240
previously unrepentant sociopaths.

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:44.880
This effect is not chemical, but psychic,
and one day it may grow powerful enough that

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:48.240
not even the Scarlet King himself will be
immune.

00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:51.600
The experiment with SCP-682 was most remarkable.

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:54.360
Based on multiple Daevite texts, including&nbsp;

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:57.960
descriptions from SCP-140&nbsp;
itself, we are reasonably

00:18:57.960 --> 00:19:01.920
certain that 682 is the offspring of the Fourth
Scarlet Bride.

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:08.520
If this is true, then SCP-999 is already strong
enough to temporarily quell the malevolence

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:10.320
of its own eldritch siblings.

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:16.560
One day 999 could very well be strong enough
to permanently reform its family members just

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:18.360
as it reforms human beings.

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:23.880
It will not overthrow the Scarlet King by
force, but with light and love and laughter

00:19:23.880 --> 00:19:26.520
that can brighten the blackest of hearts.

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:30.420
999 is not, in reality, a safe class SCP.

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:32.100
It is Thaumiel.

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:35.880
It is the best and really the only weapon
we have against some of the most powerful

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:38.160
hostile entities known to exist.

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:43.740
By all means, doctor, enjoy the relative safety
of your new position, but do keep in mind

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:47.640
that SCP-999 is not a mere pet that we fancy.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:52.140
It is one of our most valuable assets and
must be safeguarded at all costs.

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:57.240
Its safety and well-being are paramount, and
you are not at liberty to share this information

00:19:57.240 --> 00:20:01.320
to anyone without level 5/999 security clearance.

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:06.120
As per protocol, unauthorized disclosure of
level 5 classified information will result

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:07.260
in your termination.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:12.120
This e-mail will automatically delete as soon
as you leave the terminal, so feel free to

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:16.140
reread it as many times as necessary to remember
all of the pertinent information.

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:19.260
Take good care of our little tickle monster.

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:22.260
The fate of the Multiverse may well depend
on it.

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:26.520
- Your secret admirer (if anyone asks), O5-1."

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:31.980
Dr. Collingwood let out a long, slow breath
as her mind did its best to process everything

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:32.940
she just read.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:37.740
The message looked official, and, when she
really thought about it...this all made a

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:39.240
twisted kind of sense.

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:45.540
What could SCP-999 possibly be, if not some
sort of mythic hero of divine prophecy?

00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:50.340
What other explanation could there be for
something so utterly, perfectly good?

00:20:50.340 --> 00:20:55.800
Maybe one day that happy orange slime would
save them all, and do it with a smile.

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:58.980
But for now, it was just a little, innocent
child.

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:03.840
No need to burden it with talk of heroism,
of epic battles between good and evil.

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:10.380
For now, she would just pour SCP-999 a heaping
bowl of M&amp;Ms, give it a gentle pat, and say

00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:10.860
"thank you."

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:16.080
The tickle monster gurgled excitedly in response,
nuzzling his new head researcher's hand.

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:21.240
He didn't understand what she was thanking
him for, but he appreciated it all the same.

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:24.780
Now go check out “SCP-999 Tickle Monster
VS.

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:29.100
the Most Evil SCPs” and “What Does SCP-999
Do All Day?

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:33.300
(Hour by Hour)” for more knowledge about
the most adorable anomaly of all!

